{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"ae60a4ea081763dea3d127ee37123ee787a0641a09f8323b40dc19375de53d65","digest":{"component_or_area":"autolander compose service + state volume management","key_entities":["infra/compose/Dockerfile.autolander","infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","infra/scripts/compose-up.sh","gerrit_autolander","autolander.lock","willfarrell/autoheal","autoheal=true","SITE_SUBDIRS","recovery.json","volume_for_subdir()"],"problem_keywords":["autolander","container","docker compose","single-instance","state volume","flock","autoheal","gerrit"],"propositions":["The autolander service must be packaged as a Docker image (Dockerfile.autolander) and integrated into the existing compose stack as a single-instance service on the Gerrit box.","A second instance of autolander must fail to start when the first holds a POSIX file lock on autolander.lock in the mounted state volume, enforcing single-instance semantics without relying on deploy.replicas.","The named external volume gerrit_autolander must persist state across container recreation (autolander.lock, heartbeat file, emergency-stop sentinel, recovery.json) and be declared in SITE_SUBDIRS.","The willfarrell/autoheal sidecar must be wired into docker-compose.yml with read-write Docker socket access and manage the autolander service via the autoheal=true label to enable automatic restart on failure.","config-check.sh check 5 must pass when autolander is added to SITE_SUBDIRS, preventing CI drift when external volumes are declared."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785817849942847182,"uuid":"8561d32d-59b6-49e9-a99f-19d337fe0679"}